body:
Hi Vincent

So basically my app is being used in a matching system. The user will search for suitable matches and be presented by a limited amount of information. However in the results, say for example the result matched on 'eye colour'. I want to display the this is why this particular hit was presented. This is how I'd like it to work...

```
<div class="hit">
    <div class="resultReason">@{{#helpers.highlightResults}}@{{{ _highlightResult }}}@{{/helpers.highlightResults}}</div>
    <div class="result">
        <p>Name: @{{ fname }} @{{ lname }}</p>
        <p>Email: @{{ email }}</p>
        <p>Town: @{{ town }}</p>
        <p>Age: @{{ age }}</p>
        <a href="/profile/@{{ id }}">Full Profile</a>
    </div>
</div>


<script>
//
//SEARCH CODE ETC
//

search.templatesConfig.helpers.highlightResults = function (text, render){
    //loop through _highlightResult
    //
    //Create Message
    var message = "<div>This result was matched on:" + _highlightResult.title;
    //add to hit result
    return message;
}
</script>
```
